chExplorer (2)\\\" listing both authored discussions (thread-1, thread-7).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"As qatester08: set bio to \\\"QA test bio for FT-13 persistence check.\\\" and interests to Testing/Automation/QA, upvoted thread-2 (visible as bg-primary/10 text-primary active class), and posted 5 replies to thread-5 (34->39). Logged out via SPA (no reload), then logged back in with qatester08@example.com. After re-login: profile page still showed the same bio and interest tags with \\\"Edit Profile\\\" available again; thread-2 upvote button still showed active class bg-primary/10 text-primary; thread-5 still showed 39 replies. All state intact after logout/login within the same session.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-18\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"State does not persist across page reload\", \"actual\": \"Before reload: logged in as qatester08 with custom bio/interests set, thread-2 at 93 upvotes (including qatester08's vote, shown active), thread-5 at 39 replies (including 5 replies posted by qatester08). After a full page reload (browser_navigate to /), the app returned to an unauthenticated state (nav shows \\\"Login\\\"/\\\"Register\\\" links instead of the user), all upvote buttons became disabled/unauthenticated, thread-2 reverted to 89 upvotes, and thread-5 reverted to 34 replies. All accounts created and all activity (votes, replies, profile edits) performed during the session were completely lost, indicating the application only persists state in client-side memory with no backend/localStorage persistence.\", \"evidence\": \"Screenshot-free DOM snapshot before reload showed thread-2=93, thread-5=39 replies, user logged in as qatester08. After browser_navigate(http://localhost:6019/), snapshot shows Login/Register links, thread-2=89, thread-5=34 replies, all upvote buttons [disabled].\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Submitting completely empty form showed \\\"Please fill in all fields\\\" and stayed on /new-thread (no thread created). Submitting with only Title filled (no category, no body) showed the same error and did not create a thread.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-17\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Incorrect password is accepted and creates a logged-in session\", \"actual\": \"Immediately after registering qatester01 and logging out in the same SPA session, logging in with qatester01's email and a deliberately wrong password (\\\"wrongpassword\\\") succeeded: toast showed \\\"Welcome back!\\\" and the app navigated to authenticated home with the user's profile link in nav. Password was not validated for that in-memory account.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-22\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Unauthenticated access to discussion creation does not redirect to a usable sign-in screen\", \"actual\": \"While logged out, the navigation bar shows only Login/Register links (no \\\"New Thread\\\" link is exposed in the UI). Directly navigating to http://localhost:6019/new-thread as an unauthenticated user does not redirect to /login or show any sign-in prompt; instead the page renders completely blank (DOM root only contains the notifications region, no heading, form, or message). A console warning \\\"You should call navigate() in a React.useEffect(), not when your component is first rendered\\\" appears, suggesting the app attempts an improper redirect that fails, leaving the user stuck on a blank, non-functional page with no way to sign in or return to discussion creation.\", \"evidence\": \"Snapshot of http://localhost:6019/new-thread while logged out: only \\\"region Notifications alt+T\\\" present, no heading/form/login link. document.body.innerHTML confirmed root div is essentially empty. Reproduced twice.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Baseline Trending order: thread-6(156), thread-4(124), thread-7(92), thread-2(89), thread-5(78), thread-8(67), thread-3(56), thread-1(47). Using 4 distinct accounts (qatester05-08) to upvote thread-2 one at a time, its count rose 89->90->91->92->93. At 93, thread-2 reordered above thread-7(92): new order thread-6(156), thread-4(124), thread-2(93), thread-7(92), thread-5(78), thread-8(67), thread-3(56), thread-1(47). List correctly re-sorted descending by upvote count as votes changed.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-19\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"After posting a reply, thread detail top summary showed \\\"1 replies\\\" and Replies section header showed \\\"Replies (1)\\\" with exactly one reply listed - counts match.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-20\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No stated time window for Trending/Most Active views; ranking is not restricted to a recent window\", \"actual\": \"The \\\"Trending Discussions\\\" view heading/subtitle reads only \\\"Trending Discussions\\\" / \\\"Join the conversation with our community\\\" - no mention of any time window (e.g. \\\"This Week\\\", \\\"Past 24 Hours\\\", \\\"Past 30 Days\\\"). Same for \\\"Most Active Discussions\\\" view: heading/subtitle also just \\\"Most Active Discussions\\\" / \\\"Join the conversation with our community\\\" with no time-window label. Furthermore, all threads shown in both views are timestamped \\\"over 2 years ago\\\", confirming the ranking algorithm considers all-time data rather than being scoped to any recent window, and no UI text anywhere states a time window is being applied.\", \"evidence\": \"Snapshot of homepage Trending view: heading \\\"Trending Discussions\\\", paragraph \\\"Join the conversation with our community\\\". Snapshot after clicking \\\"Most Active\\\": heading \\\"Most Active Discussions\\\", same subtitle. All 8 articles' time elements read \\\"over 2 years ago\\\" in both views.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-21\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Community